  "live_records": {
    "q-73556": {
      "dom_id": "step-q73556",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Evaluate the repeated integral ${\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}3y{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{4}[{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}3y{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}3y[{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}3y{[\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{4}]}_{0}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}3y(\\frac{{e}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{e}^{0}}{4})\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{3}{4}y({e}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{3}{4}y({e}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}y & =\\frac{3}{4}({e}^{2}-1){\\int }_{2}^{4}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{3}{4}({e}^{2}-1)\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}({e}^{2}-1)(\\frac{{4}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{2}^{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}({e}^{2}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
