    "q-73578": {
      "dom_id": "step-q73578",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Evaluate the repeated integral\n${\\int }_{0}^{1/2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}[{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}[{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}{[-\\frac{1}{x}]}_{1}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}(-\\frac{1}{2}-(-1))\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\text{d}y & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡y]_{0}^{1/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{\\pi }{6}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
