    "q-37925": {
      "dom_id": "step-q37925",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "${\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}[{\\int }_{1}^{2}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}[{e}^{x+y}]_{1}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}({e}^{y+2}-{e}^{y+1})\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}({e}^{y+2}-{e}^{y+1})\\text{d}y & =[{e}^{y+2}-{e}^{y+1}]_{1}^{2} \\\\  & ={e}^{4}-{e}^{3}-({e}^{3}-{e}^{2}) \\\\  & ={e}^{4}-2{e}^{3}+{e}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
