    "q-37956": {
      "dom_id": "step-q37956",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{D}\\sqrt{{x}^{3}y}\\,\\text{d}A$, where $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,1\\le y\\le 4\\}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we express our double integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\sqrt{{x}^{3}y}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{{x}^{3}y}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{{x}^{3}y}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\sqrt{y}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\sqrt{y}{[\\frac{2}{5}{x}^{5/2}]}_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\sqrt{y}(\\frac{2}{5}(1)^{5/2}-\\frac{2}{5}(0)^{5/2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{2}{5}\\sqrt{y}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{2}{5}\\sqrt{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\frac{2}{5}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{y}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}{[\\frac{2{y}^{3/2}}{3}]}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}((4)^{3/2}-(1)^{3/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{15}(8-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{28}{15}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
