    "q-73595": {
      "dom_id": "step-q73595",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{D}\\frac{2x}{{y}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}A,$ where $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,2\\le x\\le 4,\\,1\\le y\\le 2\\}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we express our double integral as a repeated integral:      \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\frac{2x}{{y}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}[{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{2x}{{y}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}[{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{2x}{{y}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{2}{{y}^{4}}[{\\int }_{2}^{4}x\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{2}{{y}^{4}}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{2}^{4}\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{2}{{y}^{4}}(\\frac{{4}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{2}^{2}}{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{12}{{y}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{12}{{y}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}y & ={[-\\frac{4}{{y}^{3}}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{{2}^{3}}+\\frac{4}{{1}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
