    "q-72136": {
      "dom_id": "step-q72136",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "Which of the following equalities are true given that\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,-1\\le y\\le 1\\}.$\n\nI. ${∬}_{D}\\frac{x-1}{y+2}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{x-1}{y+2}\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$\n\nII. ${∬}_{D}\\frac{x-1}{y+2}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{x-1}{y+2}\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$\n\nIII. ${∬}_{D}\\frac{x-1}{y+2}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{x-1}{y+2}\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y$",
      "worked_solution": "We notice that:\n\n- the limits for the variable $x$ are from $0$ to $2$, and\n\n- the limits for the variable $y$ are from $-1$ to $1.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\frac{x-1}{y+2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{x-1}{y+2}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since the region of integration is rectangular, we can simply swap the order of integration. This gives\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}\\frac{x-1}{y+2}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{x-1}{y+2}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only\".",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-72136-a",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "I only",
              "html": "I only"
            },
            {
              "option": "b",
