><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\"><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace></mstyle><mtext>d</mtext><mi>A</mi></mtd><mtd><mi></mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"OP\">∫</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mstyle mathcolor=\"red\"><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mstyle></mrow><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mstyle mathcolor=\"red\"><mn>1</mn></mstyle></mrow></msubsup><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"INNER\"><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"OPEN\">[</mo><msubsup><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"OP\">∫</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mstyle mathcolor=\"blue\"><mn>0</mn></mstyle></mrow><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mstyle mathcolor=\"blue\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mn>2</mn></mrow></mstyle></mrow></msubsup><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\"><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace></mstyle><mtext>d</mtext><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mstyle mathcolor=\"blue\"><mi>x</mi></mstyle></mrow><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"CLOSE\">]</mo></mrow><mtext>d</mtext><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mstyle mathcolor=\"red\"><mi>y</mi></mstyle></mrow><mo>.</mo></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></p>\n<p>Now, since the region of integration is rectangular, we can simply swap the order of integration. This gives</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" display=\"true\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"141\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math display=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"margin-left: 0px; margin-right: 0px;\"><mjx-munder><mjx-row><mjx-base><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-lop\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c222C TEX-S2\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-base></mjx-row><mjx-row><mjx-under style=\"padding-top: 0.167em; padding-left: 0.152em;\"><mjx-texatom size=\"s\" texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D43